From f542041feffd365c2892a7f14a0e79b549fd5fb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Steiner <tomac@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:12:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [iOS] Run Gemma on the GPU when the app has room, and
 record its speed

Picks the GPU whenever loading the model there leaves the app at least
1.5 GB from its memory limit, and the CPU otherwise, in place of a fixed
6 GB of device memory. On an iPhone 11 Pro Max (4 GB), the GPU decodes
at 22 tokens per second against 14 on the CPU, and answers its first
token in 0.5 s against 2.3 s, at 1.2 GB of footprint against 0.6 GB.

Developer launch arguments pick the backend and the CPU thread count
(-BuiltInAIGemmaBackend, -BuiltInAIGemmaThreads), and keep the device
awake while Chrome is in front (-BuiltInAIKeepAwake). After every
answer, Gemma's speed and the app's memory footprint go to
Library/Caches/BuiltInAI/stats.jsonl.
---
 .../model/built_in_ai_engine.swift            | 122 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../model/built_in_ai_java_script_feature.h   |   4 +
 .../model/built_in_ai_java_script_feature.mm  |  13 ++
 3 files changed, 135 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

